  <iati-identifier>GB-CHC-285776-PAR019</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Civil Society and Promoting Democracy, Paraguay</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall mission of Decidamos is to contribute to the formation of a Paraguayan citizenship that is active, critical, organised, pluralist, focused on the construction of a democracy of social justice and human rights. This project aims to enable ordinary Paraguayan people to promote democratic values and to participate and engage in the country&#x2019;s future.  Decidamos have a variety of different projects funded by a variety of donors, and the project that CAFOD supports focuses on following the General Budget of Expenditure of the Nation (PGGN) and support civil society organisations as they seek to influence the budget development and implementation process. Decidamos look to improve the capacities of civil society and social organisations which aim to influence the budget development and implementation process in which social policies are established that have the objective of reducing levels of poverty. 

The project has three lines of action:	
1. To generate alternative information concerning the previous budget such as resources available in the budget, resources badly used and an investment proposal for the budget for the next year in some social areas that require investment- health, education, housing, agrarian reform, children
2. To articulate an alliance of social organisations and networks that are mobilised for demanding better and greater investment
3. Inform and sensitise citizens about the desired amount of social investment and challenges that require more efficient, effective and equitable investment. 

This year they will also be looking at the tax system and how this links to social investment.</narrative>
  </description>
